I finally beat Angband and am now playing NetHack.  Quite a different
game and a lot of fun.  I'd say maybe 20% of the knowledge transfers -
e.g., if there's a mob of monsters, back into a corridor, general sense
of when to teleport/bail, awareness of traps, last-ditch things to try
if you're about to die, etc.  Other than that kind of "common to all
roguelikes" info, it's a brave new world...

I've been playing a lot of different classes since I figure I'll have
lots of early deaths before getting to the later, more emotionally
wrenching deaths ;)  Making it to minetown semi-consistently without
dying of hunger now, so at least that's some progress...

I've read the guidebook, but still have some questions:

(a) Is there a way to see your own intrinsics?  I'm referring to, for
example, the abilities a monk gets as he progresses levels (stealth,
warning, etc.)  You get it when you die, but I can't find a way to
display it in the game (seems like "Player's Handbook" material to me).
 Or is there some magic item or tool that reveals this?

(b) How do you tunnel through walls?  Do you need a tool to do that?

(c) On a related note...I take it you can push boulders but not pull
them...correct?  Periodically I'll be going down a hallway and come to
a boulder...sometimes I can't push it or there's a monster on the other
side.  Is it possible to get stuck in the game (i.e., no down
staircase) because of a boulder?

(d) Is it just my luck or do Monks start with and find a ton of food?
All of my Cavemen so far have had to pray, but a couple of my Monks
started with a veritable smorgasboard and were finding food rations
left and right.  Is that game balance because Monks are vegetarians?

(e) Is there a way to say "rest until healed" or do you just have to
keep hitting '.'?  I've found just holding it down is too dangerous ;)

(f) How good is a character's hearing - for example, when I hear guards
on patrol or the chime of a cash register, does that always mean it's
on the same level I'm on, within +/- 1 level, within +/- 2 levels,
or...?

(g) Is there a way to target arrows/bolts?  If I'm on one side of a
room and some orc comes in the other side, I find I have to move first
to make sure I'm lined up in one of the 8 directional points before I
fire.  Is there a way to point at a target with the cursor, or...?

Thanks all!

